## Docker & Infrastructure

**Multi-stage build pattern (mandatory):**
```dockerfile
FROM golang:1.25-alpine AS builder
WORKDIR /app
COPY go.mod go.sum ./
RUN go mod download
COPY . .
RUN go build -o server ./cmd/server

FROM alpine:3.19 AS runtime
COPY --from=builder /app/server /server
EXPOSE 9000
HEALTHCHECK CMD wget -q -O- http://localhost:9000/health || exit 1
CMD ["/server"]
```

**All services must have `/health` endpoint.**

**Port mapping:**
- Dev: nginx:8080, backend:9000, graph-service:9091
- Personal: backend:8085, gateway:8082, graph-service:8092
- Test: frontend:3002, backend:8083, graph-service:9095, postgres:5434, redis:6381

**Volume names:**
- Dev: `postgres_data`, `redis_data`, `huggingface_cache`
- Personal: `pgdata_personal`, `redisdata_personal`, `mongodbdata_personal`
- Test: `pgdata_test`, `mongodbdata_test` (destroyed after use)

**Test Stack (MANDATORY for testing):**
- Use `docker-compose.test.yml` for all E2E/BDD testing
- Completely isolated from dev/personal environments
- Unique container names: `kg-test-*`
- Test database: `knowledge_test` with test credentials
- Scripts: `.\scripts\start-test.ps1`, `.\scripts\stop-test.ps1`, `.\scripts\seed-test-data.ps1`
- Always destroy with `down -v` to remove test data

